# Files legitimately built/staged under debian/tmp but not shipped in
# any ostserver binary package - see debian/ostserver.install's own
# comment on usr/lib/*/libstellarsolver6.so* for the companion runtime
# fix (Launchpad build failure, dh_missing, 2026-10-13).
#
# StellarSolver (libs/stellarsolver, vendored) is built in-tree and
# linked directly by ostserver's own CMake targets - nothing outside
# this source package ever does `find_package(StellarSolver)` against
# it, so its dev package surface (public headers, CMake config,
# pkg-config file) has no consumer here. Only the runtime .so itself
# (claimed in debian/ostserver*.install) is actually needed.
usr/include/libstellarsolver/*
usr/include/libstellarsolver/astrometry/*
usr/lib/*/cmake/StellarSolver/*
usr/lib/*/pkgconfig/stellarsolver.pc
